{
  "id": "next-greater-element-i",
  "questionId": "next-greater-element-i",
  "slug": "next-greater-element-i",
  "title": "Next Greater Element I",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Monotonic stack",
  "patterns": [
    "monotonic stack",
    "array"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "you need the 'next greater element' for every value in nums2, not just the ones in nums1 - what if you computed that for the whole array first, then just looked up the values you need?",
    "walk nums2 left to right while keeping a stack of values that are still waiting for their next greater element",
    "when the current value is greater than the value on top of the stack, that stack value has found its answer - pop it and record the mapping, and keep popping while the top is still smaller",
    "push the current value onto the stack afterward; anything left on the stack at the end never found a next greater element, so its answer is -1. store all mappings in a hash map, then look up each nums1 value"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "re-scanning nums2 from scratch for every nums1 query instead of precomputing once",
    "comparing values with >= instead of > when popping the stack, which would treat an equal value as 'greater'",
    "forgetting that stack values left over at the end map to -1"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two arrays of distinct integers, `nums1` and `nums2`, where every value in `nums1` also appears somewhere in `nums2`. `nums2` may be longer than `nums1`.\n\n**For each value in `nums1`, find the first element to its right in `nums2` that is strictly greater than it, using -1 if no such element exists, and return the results in the same order as `nums1`.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= nums1.length <= nums2.length <= 1000",
      "0 <= nums1[i], nums2[i] <= 10^4",
      "all integers in nums1 are distinct, and all integers in nums2 are distinct",
      "nums1 is a subset of nums2"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "the queried value is the last element of nums2 (no next greater element)",
      "nums1 has only one element",
      "nums2 is strictly increasing (every query has a next greater element right after it)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
